What the CC BY-NC license does and does not cover
-------------------------------------------------
The license applies to the authors' own contributions: the synthetic text,
the labels/annotations, the baselines, and the selection and arrangement of
the dataset. It does NOT, and cannot, grant any rights in third-party
trademarks, trade names, or publicity rights (Creative Commons licenses do not
license trademark or patent rights).

Synthetic content & trademark notice
------------------------------------
All 800 descriptions are AI-GENERATED for research. The 400 real-product items
reference real brands and companies (e.g. Colgate Total, Pampers Swaddlers,
Procter & Gamble); the text — marketing copy, "user reviews," and the
"patent"/"regulatory" passages — and the numeric specifications are FABRICATED.
They are NOT real copy, reviews, claims, patents, filings, or statements by
those brands and may be factually inaccurate. All brand, product, and company
names are the trademarks of their respective owners and are used nominatively
for non-commercial research only. No affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement
is implied or intended. The remaining 400 items use entirely fictional names.

Takedown
--------
Rights holders who would like any item removed may open an issue at
https://github.com/adromero/langprod/issues and it will be addressed promptly.
